# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in, then `docker compose --env-file .env up --build`
# or export these in your shell before `docker compose up`.

# --- Email OTP delivery (auth-service) ---
# Gmail SMTP + an App Password (see backend/README.md for how to obtain one).
# Any other SMTP provider (SendGrid, Mailgun, SES) works too — just change these.
RISKYC_MAIL_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
RISKYC_MAIL_PORT=587
RISKYC_MAIL_USERNAME=your-address@gmail.com
RISKYC_MAIL_PASSWORD=your-16-character-app-password
RISKYC_MAIL_FROM=your-address@gmail.com

# --- Media (media-service) ---
# media-service issues MinIO pre-signed URLs using this as the host part —
# it MUST be reachable from wherever the client (phone) actually is, not
# just from inside the docker network. Left at localhost, every image/voice
# message/video URL would 404 on any device other than the host machine
# itself. On the VPS this needs to be the public IP/domain, at whatever
# host port MinIO's S3 API is actually published on (MINIO_API_HOST_PORT
# below — 9010 by default here, NOT MinIO's usual 9000, since this VPS
# already has another MinIO container bound to 9000/9001).
RISKYC_MINIO_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT=http://167.86.120.214:9010

# --- Host port overrides ---
# The defaults below are already shifted off the "usual" ports on purpose:
# `docker ps` on the target VPS showed 5432, 8080, 8081, 8082, 8443, 9000,
# and 9001 already bound by other stacks (riskyc-backend, nguon-app, jitsi).
# Everything here uses a free port instead, so this stack starts cleanly
# alongside them with zero edits. Only touch these if a *future* deploy
# target has a different set of ports already taken — docker will refuse to
# start and say "address already in use" if so, never silently conflict.
# If you change MINIO_API_HOST_PORT, update RISKYC_MINIO_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT's
# port above to match, since that's what the mobile client actually uses.
# POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=5433
# REDIS_HOST_PORT=6379
# MINIO_API_HOST_PORT=9010
# MINIO_CONSOLE_HOST_PORT=9011
# AUTH_SERVICE_HOST_PORT=8091
# MESSAGING_SERVICE_HOST_PORT=8092
# MEDIA_SERVICE_HOST_PORT=8083
# PRESENCE_SERVICE_HOST_PORT=8084

# --- TURN relay for calling (coturn) ---
# Needed for audio/video calls to actually connect once caller and callee
# are on different networks — public STUN alone frequently can't find a
# working P2P path (the call "rings" and "connects" but no media ever
# arrives). TURN_EXTERNAL_IP must be the VPS's real public IP — coturn
# advertises this as the relay address, so it's wrong on any other host.
# The username/password are a static long-lived credential — change them
# from the defaults if you're deploying this for real, since a decompiled
# APK reveals them, but they only grant relay access (not backend access).
# TURN_PORT=3478
# TURN_USERNAME=riskyc
# TURN_PASSWORD=riskyc-turn-secret
# TURN_EXTERNAL_IP=167.86.120.214
# TURN_RELAY_MIN_PORT=49160
# TURN_RELAY_MAX_PORT=49200
